  "_note": "Sites \u2014 the fourth layer (docs/sites-system.md). Things a world CONTAINS, as opposed to things it IS. Conditions are ranges, never exact matches, so a family of worlds can produce a given site and sites are hunted by understanding conditions rather than memorising a recipe. Rarity is emergent: a site needing three simultaneous uncommon conditions is rare because that world is hard to write. All numbers PLACEHOLDER. Q17: ruins pay in KNOWLEDGE and OBJECTS, never currency \u2014 landmarks and living sites pay in materials. And a ruin is never empty: knowledge first, an object always, so a ruin whose knowledge you already hold is still worth the walk. Gear is FOUND, never researched (session 12 \u00a74): ordinary gear comes from encounters and common finds, notably better gear from sites \u2014 especially ruins, where it reads as something left behind by someone.",
